    "result": "I implemented `compare_versions` in `solution.py` and wrote a 69-case pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. The implementation parses each version with regexes (no leading zeros in core or numeric prerelease identifiers, `ValueError` on any malformed input), ignores build metadata, and compares core numbers, then release vs. prerelease, then prerelease identifiers left to right with numeric identifiers ranking below alphanumeric ones and shorter prerelease lists ranking lower. The tests cover precedence ordering, build-metadata equivalence, antisymmetry, and a broad set of invalid inputs. I did not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation, or bandit gates, since the only permitted command was the test run, so those are unverified.",
